# Protected branches (test mode)

Humans own merges and deploys for ~1–2 months. GitHub branch rulesets may be unavailable on this private org (no Team plan) — this rule is mandatory for Cursor/agents anyway.

## Never
- Merge into `main`, `master`, or `develop` (no merge button/API, no squash/rebase onto those branches).
- Push commits directly to `main`, `master`, or `develop`.
- Force-push or delete `main`, `master`, or `develop`.
- Deploy, release, publish stores, or tag production.
- Bypass branch protection or ask the user to weaken GitHub App permissions for merging.

## Always
- Work on a feature branch (or the existing docs branch for this PR).
- Open or update a PR that targets the correct integration branch.
- Stop when the PR is ready for **human review**.
- Reply with the PR URL; the user or their developers will merge and deploy manually.
